From 95b83ca2414a2ce40a0bf987688a49d8511133f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:24:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(post): generic LinuxCNC 3-axis mill post and machine

A new built-in post "LinuxCNC" (assets/posts/linuxcnc.cps, .ngc) and a
generic machine "LinuxCNC 3-axis", written from the public LinuxCNC 2.9
G-code and M-code references, structured after our own tormach.cps with
the PathPilot assumptions removed.

- Retract option: G53 G0 Z<safe_retract> from the machine file (refused
  by name when unstated - never an assumed G53 G0 Z0, #435/#495), G91
  G28/G30 Z0 (Z only), or none.
- T<n> M6 then G43 H<n>; option to leave G43 (and the section G49) out
  when the M6 remap applies the length.
- G64 P<tolerance> or G61; M30 or M2; optional % delimiters; G91.1
  stated; arcs and helices with incremental IJK.
- G73/G81/G82/G83/G85/G86/G89 with G99; a floating-holder tap is G84;
  a rigid tap is G33.1 Z K, only on a machine that states
  rigid_tapping true (encoder), else refused by name.
- Refused by name: control compensation, tilted moves, home after an
  operation, non-positive tool numbers, G73/G83 with Q <= 0.

The machine mirror now also publishes rigidTappingStated (true only for
a stated rigid_tapping: true), since rigidTapping reads unstated as true.

Pinned by linuxcnc_post (9 tests), conformance (linuxcnc goldens),
script_linuxcnc, and the cross-post suites cycle_hop, ream_cycle, comp,
control_comp, wear_comp, post_spindle_rule_all, machine.

Fixes #2303

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
